          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#for_directed_spaces For directed spaces
          %p
            In generalization to how a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            whose
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            = succeed "-classes" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            operation is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concatenation"} concatenation
            of paths, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+space"} directed space
            has a
            %strong fundamental category
            whose morphisms are
            %em directed
            paths in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#for_stratified_spaces For stratified spaces
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space"} stratified space
            has a ‘fundamental
            = succeed "\u2019," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-category+with+duals"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-category with duals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"}
              fundamental
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            of a plain old space. When a path crosses a codimension-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            stratum, “something interesting happens” – i.e., a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/catastrophe"} catastrophe
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dual
          %p
            See Café
            %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2006/11/this_weeks_finds_in_mathematic_2.html#c006196"} discussion
            and paper it inspired,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Woolf"} J. Woolf
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.3322"} Transversal homotopy theory
          %h3#for_simplicial_sets For simplicial sets
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo :
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N:Cat \to SSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            to a category, is sometimes called the
            %em fundamental category
            functor. One notation for it is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} freely generated
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            are 0-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
            are 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            (the source and target are defined by the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/face+maps"} face maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∼
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^0(x) \sim id_x
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X_0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∼
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^1(x) \sim d^0(x) \circ d^2(x)
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^i
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degeneracy+map"} degeneracy
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/face+maps"} face maps
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicategory"} quasicategory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
